nforces Conventional Commits 1.0.0 format for commit messages Supports scopes such as rust-core, py-binding, and ts-binding Handles nested lists in Markdown output Exposes sanitization options to Python API via py-binding Utilizes pre-commit hooks for quality assurance Streams parsers for 56+ document formats git-standards is a set of guidelines for committing code changes using Conventional Commits 1.0.0, ensuring high-quality and readable commit history');
